# ======================================================================
# FRONTEND env example (React + Vite).
# Copy to `.env` for LOCAL DEV only. Never commit the real `.env`.
#
# ── PRODUCTION (Vercel) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Put these in the Vercel dashboard → Settings → Environment Variables.
# They are read at build time; Vercel redeploys after a change.
#
#   BACKEND_API_KEY
#       Server-only secret. MUST equal Render's AI_SERVICE_KEY.
#       The edge middleware (middleware.js) reads this and injects it as
#       `X-API-Key` on /api/chat/* and /api/contact before rewriting the
#       request to the Render backend. Missing → the middleware fails
#       closed with HTTP 503 (by design).
#
#   ⚠️  NEVER set VITE_BACKEND_URL (or any VITE_*) in the Vercel env.
#       Vite inlines every VITE_* variable into the public JS bundle.
#       Setting VITE_BACKEND_URL makes the browser call the Render backend
#       directly WITHOUT the X-API-Key header → HTTP 401 on /chat, and it
#       leaks the backend URL (and any VITE_API_KEY you set) into the
#       bundle. This is the #1 cause of the chat "401 Unauthorized".
#
# ── LOCAL DEV ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Point the dev server at your local FastAPI instance (auth is skipped
# when the backend runs with ENV=development):
#   cd ai_service && venv/bin/uvicorn app:app --reload
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Backend connection (local dev only; keep unset in production) ---
VITE_BACKEND_URL=http://localhost:8000

# --- Backend vars (see ai_service/.env.example) ---
# GROQ_API_KEY=...
# GEMINI_API_KEY=...
# AI_SERVICE_KEY=...   (used only by the backend; never expose client-side)
# RESEND_API_KEY=...
